  "scope": "Select a nerve level to compare a sensory landmark with a representative motor action. Dots mark approximate examination landmarks on an original schematic; they do not outline complete dermatome territories. Examine both sides.",
  "limits": "Dermatomes overlap and vary between people. Muscles receive multiple roots; a key-muscle level is a clinical convention. C1 has no usual cutaneous dermatome. Thoracic and sacral levels without a listed key muscle still contribute motor innervation. This reference does not calculate an ASIA impairment grade.",
  "mri_notes": [
    "Correlate the side and clinical distribution with the level, compartment and severity of neural compression on MRI. A sensory level may reflect cord disease rather than a single root lesion.",
    "Confirm vertebral numbering, including transitional anatomy. Disc level, exiting root, traversing root and spinal cord segment are different labels.",
    "At L4–5, a subarticular disc lesion typically affects the traversing L5 root; a foraminal or extraforaminal lesion may affect the exiting L4 root.",
    "Cervical roots C1–C7 exit above their same-numbered vertebrae; C8 exits at C7–T1. Thoracic and lumbar roots exit below their same-numbered vertebrae."
  ],
